@backendUrl = https://localhost:7289
@aiUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8001
@candidateEmail =candidate@gmail.com
@candidatePassword = 111111Aa@
@serviceToken = ccadf1fcb245c6d59a92c6b4770e207d21298d2614cd09ce37c650586b7ade34
@cvFilePath = C:\Users\truon\Downloads\CV.pdf

# MF-02 -> MF-03 real local flow.
# This file uses the normal HRConnect database and the configured R2 bucket.
# It does NOT use hr_connect_e2e.

# Before running:
# 1. Start ai-service on port 8001 and HRConnect on https://localhost:7289.
# 2. Both services must use the same HRCONNECT_SERVICE_TOKEN.
# 3. Replace serviceToken above without committing the secret.
# 4. Confirm cvFilePath points to your PDF.
# 5. Run requests in order. TC-03 automatically obtains a usable Job ID.

### TC-00 - AI process is alive; expect HTTP 200
GET {{aiUrl}}/health

### TC-00B - AI has the HR Connect integration settings; expect HTTP 200
GET {{aiUrl}}/ready

### TC-01 - Candidate login; expect HTTP 200
# @name candidateLogin
POST {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{candidateEmail}}",
  "password": "{{candidatePassword}}"
}

### TC-02 - Inspect all ACTIVE Jobs visible to this Candidate; expect HTTP 200
# This request is informational. It proves the account can see submit-enabled service types.
GET {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/jobs?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### TC-03 - Automatically select the seeded CV_APPLICATION Job; expect items[0].jobId
# @name candidateJobs
GET {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/jobs?search=%5BSEED%5D%20Full%20Stack%20.NET%20Developer%20-%20CV%20Sourcing&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### TC-04 - Verify the selected Job before uploading; expect HTTP 200
GET {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/{{candidateJobs.response.body.$.items[0].jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### TC-05 - Upload the real PDF and create Submission/Application; expect HTTP 200
# Expected response: success=true and data.aiStatus=PENDING.
# @name candidateApply
POST {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/jobs/{{candidateJobs.response.body.$.items[0].jobId}}/apply
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=MF03RealBoundary

--MF03RealBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="CV.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< {{cvFilePath}}
--MF03RealBoundary--

### TC-06 - Verify HR Connect can create the temporary R2 download URL; expect HTTP 200
GET {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/internal/cvs/{{candidateApply.response.body.$.data.cvId}}/download-url
X-Service-Token: {{serviceToken}}

### TC-07 - Verify the Job/JD payload consumed by MF-03; expect HTTP 200
GET {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/internal/jobs/{{candidateJobs.response.body.$.items[0].jobId}}/jd
X-Service-Token: {{serviceToken}}

### TC-08 - Read the AI result
# The first response can be PENDING or PROCESSING.
# Re-run only TC-08 after a few seconds until status is COMPLETED or FAILED.
GET {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/internal/ai-results/{{candidateApply.response.body.$.data.applicationId}}
X-Service-Token: {{serviceToken}}

### TC-09 - Security check with an invalid service token; expect HTTP 403
GET {{backendUrl}}/api/v1/internal/ai-results/{{candidateApply.response.body.$.data.applicationId}}
X-Service-Token: wrong-secret

# If TC-05 returns HTTP 409, this Candidate already applied to the selected Job.
# If that Job becomes unavailable, replace the encoded search text in TC-03
# with another Candidate-visible ACTIVE Job title.
